.TH BOOP 1 "September 2026" "boop 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boop \- detach a program from its terminal and reattach later
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boop
.RB [ \-\-session
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-detach\-key
.IR key ]
.RI [ command " [" arg ...]]
.br
.B boop \-\-name
.I name
.RB [ \-\-detach\-key
.IR key ]
.br
.B boop \-\-disconnect
.I name
.br
.B boop \-\-list
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boop
runs a command in a session that outlives the terminal.
Any number of terminals may attach to a session.
Output goes to every attached terminal; input comes from any of them.
.PP
Without arguments,
.B boop
starts
.B $SHELL
in the session
.B boop
when no session runs,
attaches to the session when one runs,
and lists the sessions when several run.
.PP
With a
.IR command ,
.B boop
starts it in the session
.B boop
or the session given by
.BR \-\-session .
The session must not exist.
.PP
A session ends when its command exits.
Attached terminals then exit with the command's status,
or 128 plus the signal number if a signal ended it.
.PP
Attaching resizes the session to the terminal and signals the session as if resized.
Mouse, colour and other terminal modes pass through unchanged,
and are reset in the terminal on detach.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-session " \fIname\fR"
Attach to session
.IR name ,
or start it.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " \fIname\fR"
Attach to the existing session
.IR name .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-disconnect " \fIname\fR"
Detach every terminal from session
.IR name .
The session keeps running.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
Print the name of each session.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-detach\-key " \fIkey\fR"
Detach on
.IR key ,
written as a caret and a character, for example
.BR ^A .
The default is
.BR ^\e .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.PP
Session names hold up to 64 letters, digits and the characters
.B ._\-+@:
and do not start with a dot.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BOOP_DETACH_KEY
Detach key used when
.B \-\-detach\-key
is absent.
.TP
.B BOOP_SESSION
Set to the session name for programs in a session.
.B boop
refuses to attach to the session it runs in.
.TP
.B SHELL
Command started when none is given.
Defaults to
.BR /bin/sh .
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Sessions live in
.BR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/boop ,
or in
.BI /tmp/boop\- uid
when unset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on detach, the command's status when the session ends, and 1 on error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B boop
Start or resume a shell.
.TP
.B boop \-\-session mail mutt
Run
.B mutt
in session
.BR mail .
.TP
.B boop \-\-disconnect mail
Detach other terminals from
.BR mail .
